{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>But if a man acts intentionally, etc.</b> In the Sifrei (Mekhilta here) this is their language: ״לָמוּת״ — and not to judge, and not to flog, and not to exile. And this is the reason for Joab, who fled to the altar and took hold, etc. — even though Solomon did not kill him except by law, and as the Tosafot wrote at the end of chapter Nigmar HaDin (Sanhedrin 49a) that he was in rebellion against the kingdom, he fled before the trial. And they said in HaGolin (Makkot 12a) that his error was that it was not an altar of [stones fit for the] eternal [covenant], and also that he grasped its horns, and it does not grant protection except for its roof." "<b>And I saw</b> in the Rambam, who wrote in chapter 5 of Hilkhot Rotze'ach uShmirat Nefesh, that the altar protects an unintentional murderer with regard to death at the hand of the blood avenger, but not with regard to exile — thus far. And it is certain that he did not see the baraita that infers from ״לָמוּת״ — and not to exile, and not, etc. And although one could force an interpretation to reconcile their saying ״and not to exile,״ that the intention concerns one who is liable to exile, that the blood avenger may not kill him — this interpretation is forced, and it is also contradicted by what precedes it, ״and not to judge and not to flog,״ and understand this. And the difficulty is very great to me according to the Rav, the author of the Mishneh laMelekh, who wrote and expressed wonder at the Rambam for distinguishing between unintentional and intentional, even with regard to death at the hand of the blood avenger, and said that there is no distinction at all between unintentional and intentional — thus far. And his words are not clear even without the baraita, for we cannot say that the altar protects only in that which the verse explicitly excludes."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:54.510958417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}